From 9129c185b267f8546c1e16f5605a0fe4edb670dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 14:50:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] test: the first tests in this repository, aimed at what
 was actually broken
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

npm test — 49 tests, ~25s, no database, no network, no browser, no new
dependency. Blocking in CI.

There were no tests here at all. That is how migrations/001 came to store
eleven telemetry event types while lib/validators.ts accepted fifteen, losing
100% of the 1 Hz pressure stream. It was a two-line difference between two
files in the same repository, and it survived a dedicated product-truth audit
that cited both of them, because nothing compared them. audit/scripts/ sweeps
the rendered site; none of it can see a database, an auth boundary or a
telemetry event.

  contract/event-vocabulary       TypeScript, the validator and the migration
                                  series agree. The SQL is parsed, so what is
                                  checked is the artefact the database is built
                                  from.
  contract/job-state-machine      lib/jobState.ts and the migration-002 trigger
                                  encode the same nine rules.
  telemetry/ingest                the delivery contract: auth, per-robot
                                  scoping, cross-tenant refusal, idempotent
                                  replay, poison-event isolation,
                                  dead-lettering, resume, batch limits, clock
                                  skew.
  telemetry/simulator-contract    a whole simulated job — two machines,
                                  thousands of events, chunked and
                                  authenticated — through the real ingest path
                                  with nothing refused and everything stamped
                                  `simulated`.

Verified against the defect: reverting the four ALTER TYPE lines in migration
002 turns three of these red, naming the exact four event types.

Two source changes were needed to run tests against the real modules rather
than a compiled copy that could drift from them. tsconfig sets
`erasableSyntaxOnly`, so tsc refuses syntax Node cannot strip, and the three
error classes lost their TypeScript parameter properties. That plus twenty
lines of module resolver is the whole harness — the alternative was vitest or
jest and a transform pipeline, to test a codebase whose entire build is one
`next build`.

Two bugs surfaced while writing them. isJobStatus used `value in
JOB_TRANSITIONS`, which walks the prototype chain, so "constructor" and
"toString" read as valid job statuses — in the function PATCH /api/jobs/[id]
uses to decide whether a caller-supplied string may be written. And
lib/telemetry/ingest.ts had literal NUL bytes as composite-key separators,
which made the file binary to grep and diff; they are JSON-encoded keys now.

